kluft Sand Dunes (2011).jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Namib-Naukluft_Sand_Dunes_%282011%29.jpg/960px-Namib-Naukluft_Sand_Dunes_%282011%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namib-Naukluft_Sand_Dunes_(2011).jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Sand dunes in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Namib-Naukluft_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Namib-Naukluft National Park\">Namib-Naukluft National Park</a>, Namibia. Older dunes are reddish and larger, newer dunes are yellow-brown."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"20 April 2011 (07:52:54)"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Yathin_sk\" title=\"User:Yathin sk\">Yathin S Krishnappa</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":43146708,"title":"File:Nacunda nighthawk.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Nacunda_nighthawk.jpg/960px-Nacunda_nighthawk.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nacunda_nighthawk.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nacunda_nighthawk\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Nacunda nighthawk\">Nacunda nighthawk</a>"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2015-07-31"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://photo-natur.de\">Andreas Trepte</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":46443045,"title":"File:Naha Okinawa Japan Shuri-Castle-02.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Naha_Okinawa_Japan_Shuri-Castle-02.jpg/960px-Naha_Okinawa_Japan_Shuri-Castle-02.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naha_Okinawa_Japan_Shuri-Castle-02.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Naha, Okinawa, Japan:Hoshimmon (Kimihokori-Ujo) Gate to the inner yard of Shuri Castle."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-01-05"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Cccefalon\" title=\"User:Cccefalon\">CEphoto, Uwe Aranas</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}}]},{"pageid":52061183,"title":"File:Naghsh-e rostam, Irán, 2016-09-24, DD 12.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Naghsh-e_rostam%2C_Ir%C3%A1n%2C_2016-09-24%2C_DD_12.jpg/960px-Naghsh-e_rostam%2C_Ir%C3%A1n%2C_2016-09-24%2C_DD_12.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naghsh-e_rostam,_Ir%C3%A1n,_2016-09-24,_DD_12.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shapur_I%27s_victory_relief_at_Naqsh-e_Rostam\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Shapur I's victory relief at Naqsh-e Rostam\">Relief of triumph of Shapur I over Valerian</a> at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naqsh-e_Rostam\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Naqsh-e Rostam\">Naqsh-e Rostam</a> (ca. 241–272 AD), located 3 km north of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persepolis\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Persepolis\">Persepolis</a>. It is the most impressive of eight <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sasanian\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Sasanian\">Sasanian</a> rock carvings cut into the cliff beneath the tombs of their <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achaemenid\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Achaemenid\">Achaemenid</a> predecessors. This carving depicts a famous scene in which the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Emperor\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Roman Emperor\">Roman Emperor</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valerian_(emperor)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Valerian (emperor)\">Valerian</a>, is kneeling before <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shapur_I\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Shapur I\">Shapur I</a> and asking for mercy. Shapur defeated Valerian at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Edessa\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Battle of Edessa\">Battle of Edessa</a>, in which the entire Roman army was destroyed and Valerian became Shapour's prisoner. This was the first and only time a Roman emperor was taken prisoner. The Emperor <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_the_Arab\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Philip the Arab\">Philip the Arab</a> is depicting standing and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gordian_III\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Gordian III\">Gordian III</a> is dead at the feet of Shapur's horse."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-09-24 12:04:48"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q28147777\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q28147777\"><span title=\"Spanish photographer\">Diego Delso</span></a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":52061199,"title":"File:Naghsh-e rostam, Irán, 2016-09-24, DD 20-24 PAN.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Naghsh-e_rostam%2C_Ir%C3%A1n%2C_2016-09-24%2C_DD_20-24_PAN.jpg/960px-Naghsh-e_rostam%2C_Ir%C3%A1n%2C_2016-09-24%2C_DD_20-24_PAN.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naghsh-e_rostam,_Ir%C3%A1n,_2016-09-24,_DD_20-24_PAN.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"This is a photo of a monument in Iran identified by the ID"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-09-24 12:10:22"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q28147777\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q28147777\"><span title=\"Spanish photographer\">Diego Delso</span></a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":82323553,"title":"File:Nabburg Neusath Freilandmuseum